---
import Story from '../../../layouts/Story.astro';
import ProjectMedia from '../../../components/ProjectMedia.astro';
import vehicle from '../../../assets/projects/baja-workshop.webp';
---
<Story
  route="baja"
  title="Building our first off-road vehicle · Vignesh Mayandia Chandran"
  description="Captaining 25 students through the design and fabrication of their first BAJA off-road vehicle, across five engineering groups."
  context="BAJA / Student off-road vehicle project"
  h1="Building our first off-road vehicle"
  standfirst="During my mechanical engineering degree, I captained 25 students entering BAJA, a student off-road vehicle competition, for the first time. I led the vehicle’s design and fabrication across five engineering groups."
  snapshot={[
    { label: 'Setting', value: 'Undergraduate mechanical engineering project, 2017–2018.' },
    { label: 'Team', value: '25 students building their first BAJA vehicle.' },
    { label: 'My responsibility', value: 'Technical leadership of the full design and fabrication.' },
    { label: 'Outcome', value: 'Passed the design round and built the vehicle; disqualified after failing the brake test.' },
  ]}
  nav={[
    { href: '#lead-the-build', label: 'Leading the build' },
    { href: '#design-to-vehicle', label: 'Design to vehicle' },
    { href: '#brake-test', label: 'The brake test' },
  ]}
>
  <section id="lead-the-build" aria-labelledby="lead-the-build-title">
    <h2 class="section-title" id="lead-the-build-title">Learning enough to lead the build</h2>
    <div class="prose">
      <p>I was chosen as captain for my ability to lead the team. Taking that responsibility meant learning each vehicle system quickly enough to understand the engineering decisions and lead the work through fabrication.</p>
      <p>I organized the team into five groups responsible for transmission, suspension, steering, brakes and the frame. My own place was in transmission, which carries power from the engine to the wheels. Across the team, my responsibility was to bring those separately designed systems together into one vehicle we could build. That required understanding what each group needed from the others, including where their parts would fit and connect.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section id="design-to-vehicle" aria-labelledby="design-to-vehicle-title">
    <h2 class="section-title" id="design-to-vehicle-title">Turning the designs into a vehicle</h2>
    <div class="prose">
      <p>We made a complete 3D model of the vehicle with exact dimensions and mounting points, then fabricated the parts to that specification. The model brought the five groups’ work together and gave us a shared basis for making parts that would fit into the same vehicle.</p>
      <p>After passing the design round, we carried the project through fabrication and assembly. I led the engineering across the groups while fundraising continued to support the build. We completed the vehicle and took it to competition.</p>
    </div>
    <ProjectMedia id="workshop-photo" src={vehicle} label="workshop photo" alt="The team's yellow-framed off-road vehicle in a workshop, with its seat, steering wheel, suspension, and wheels visible." caption="Our first BAJA vehicle during assembly, with the engine, steering and suspension fitted." />
  </section>

  <section id="brake-test" aria-labelledby="brake-test-title">
    <h2 class="section-title" id="brake-test-title">The brake test</h2>
    <div class="prose">
      <p>Before entering the driving events, the vehicle had to pass the brake test. Ours failed, and we were disqualified. Our competition entry ended before we could race.</p>
    </div>
  </section>
</Story>
